## Usage

```ts
import { Slugger, slugify, type SlugError } from "{{project_slug}}";

slugify("Hello, World!"); // "hello-world"
slugify("Hello brave new world", { separator: "_", maxLength: 11 }); // "hello_brave"

try {
  slugify("   ");
} catch (error) {
  console.log((error as SlugError).code); // "empty_input"
}

// A Slugger holds WebAssembly memory: `using` frees it at the end of the block.
{
  using headings = new Slugger();
  headings.slug("Intro"); // "intro"
  headings.slug("Intro"); // "intro-2"
}
```

The package is ES modules that import the `.wasm` file directly, which bundlers (Vite with a WebAssembly plugin, webpack, Rollup) and current Node load.

## Errors

Every function throws an `Error` named `SlugError` with a stable `code`:

| Code | When |
| --- | --- |
| `empty_input` | The input is empty or only whitespace |
| `empty_result` | The input has no letters or digits |
| `invalid_option` | An option is unknown, has the wrong type or is out of range; `field` names it |

